    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d400">

                <pb facs="0602" n="528" xml:id="pg528"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Williams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 33.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>, </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-07-30"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 30, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your despatch of the 12th of April last,
                    No. 30, in regard to the desecration of the American cemetery at Tangchau, has
                    been received.</p>
                <p>I will thank you to inform me what is the custom of guarding foreign cemeteries
                    in China; whether the government charges itself with the duty, or is it assumed
                    by foreign residents, or their consuls. You may make inquiries, and send me a
                    careful report upon the whole subject.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">S. Wells Williams</hi>, Esq.,<hi
                            rendition="#italic"> &amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
